(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// posix's identities, groups and the rest of its Linux calls (PY6e; Modules/posixmodule.c): the set*id family with"] [13 1 "// CPython's uid and gid converters, getres[ug]id from /proc/self/status (Go's syscall has no getresuid),"] [14 1 "// getgrouplist and initgroups over /etc/group as musl reads it, preadv and pwritev as one pread or pwrite per"] [15 1 "// buffer (no iovec without pointers; their RWF_* flags accepted, not applied), posix_fallocate, posix_fadvise,"] [16 1 "// lockf over fcntl's struct flock as musl's lockf, the scheduler's priority bounds (sched_getscheduler is musl's"] [17 1 "// ENOSYS), eventfd, pidfd_open, ctermid, getlogin, putenv's and unsetenv's checks and _create_environ."] [19 1 "// idConv is _Py_Uid_Converter and _Py_Gid_Converter: an int of uid_t, -1 the \"unchanged\" value."] [32 2 "// CPython's wording: past C's long \"greater than maximum\", else outside uid_t \"less than minimum\""] [42 1 "// procStatusIds are /proc/self/status's line's four ids (real, effective, saved, file system)."] [63 1 "// groupList is getgrouplist(3) as musl answers it: the group, then every group of /etc/group naming the user."] [89 1 "// writableBytes is a writable buffer's bytes: a bytearray, or a memoryview of one (one dimension, step 1)."] [107 1 "// waitidResult is waitid_result of child p's wait status st: si_code CLD_EXITED, CLD_KILLED, CLD_DUMPED,"] [108 1 "// CLD_STOPPED or CLD_CONTINUED and its si_status."] [110 37 "// CLD_EXITED"] [113 38 "// CLD_KILLED"] [115 13 "// CLD_DUMPED"] [118 42 "// CLD_STOPPED"] [120 42 "// CLD_CONTINUED"] [126 1 "// waitidNoWait is waitid(P_PID, pid, WEXITED | WNOWAIT [| WNOHANG]) without the system call (its siginfo_t takes a"] [127 1 "// pointer): the child left a zombie, its wait status read from /proc/PID/stat (state Z, exit_code: the status as"] [128 1 "// waitpid reports it); until it exits, a pidfd of it (pidfd_open) waited on by epoll, the GIL released. ECHILD when"] [129 1 "// pid is no child of this process (no /proc entry, another parent)."] [137 60 "// from field 3, state"] [142 33 "// field 52, exit_code"] [148 59 "// SYS_pidfd_open, the same on amd64 and arm64"] [181 2 "// waitid over wait4 (no siginfo_t without pointers): P_ALL, P_PID, P_PGID; WEXITED, WSTOPPED, WCONTINUED and"] [182 2 "// WNOHANG as wait4's options; si_uid the caller's, si_signo SIGCHLD. WNOWAIT (asyncio's _ThreadedChildWatcher:"] [183 2 "// no asyncio subprocess ended without it) for P_PID and WEXITED alone: waitidNoWait"] [202 11 "// P_ALL"] [203 11 "// P_PID"] [205 11 "// P_PGID"] [214 29 "// WNOWAIT"] [228 71 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [345 2 "// ---- descriptors"] [391 47 "// SEEK_CUR, from the offset on"] [483 2 "// copy_file_range and splice: the system calls when no offset is given; an offset as pread from it or pwrite"] [484 2 "// at it (the calls need a pointer to it), the descriptor's own offset left alone as the calls leave it"] [541 22 "// SYS_copy_file_range: amd64's, arm64's 285 (not in Go's syscall tables)"] [548 2 "// ---- the scheduler"] [568 44 "// musl's sched_getscheduler"] [571 2 "// ---- eventfd, pidfd_open"] [655 71 "// SYS_pidfd_open, the same on amd64 and arm64"] [663 3 "// musl's getlogin: $LOGNAME"] [670 2 "// ---- the environment"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[21 22] [166 48] [191 24] [309 36] [352 24] [380 122] [395 67] [431 34] [501 25] [565 57] [632 13] [632 20] [664 38] [673 23] [675 27] [678 32]]} (go/file "builtins_posix_ids.go" :imports [


